# Directed FU test: independent ALU work overlapping a divide.
# The three addi's don't touch the divide's registers, so they issue
# and finish while the non-pipelined divider is still busy; a long
# operation only holds up work that needs its result. The final add
# does need the quotient, so it alone waits.
# Expected output: 45, exit 0.
05400093   # addi x1, x0, 84
00200113   # addi x2, x0, 2
0220C1B3   # div  x3, x1, x2      42, occupies the divider
00100213   # addi x4, x0, 1       independent work
00120213   # addi x4, x4, 1       ...flows past the divide
00120213   # addi x4, x4, 1       x4 = 3
004182B3   # add  x5, x3, x4      45, waits for the quotient
00028513   # addi x10, x5, 0
00100893   # addi x17, x0, 1      syscall 1: print integer
00000073   # ecall                prints 45
00000513   # addi x10, x0, 0
05D00893   # addi x17, x0, 93     syscall 93: exit
00000073   # ecall
